# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL (steps/defects.md), a required positive, red: a copied method's DECLARED Structure
# formal.  b1, a copy of Box, holds getq's own occurrence under a copy of the unit; `b1\getq(w)` admits w to the
# caller's rendering of getq's formal type, while that occurrence's body reads q through the Wide of its own node:
# "a field of a formal admitted by name is not carried by its value", natively and walked -- on HEAD too.  The free
# input of the same occurrence is admitted in its own space (unit_merge_parent_model_method).  Exit 7.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
fn: getq (Wide: q) int
    return: q\x
end: getq
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: getq
end: Box
b1: merge: Box
w: merge: Wide
w\x: 4
int: r b1\getq(w)
int: ok 7
if: r != 4
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
